cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite Version 0.1.0 of this research repository."
title: "An update to the census: symmetric Hadamard matrices of order 4356"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/symmetric-hadamard-4356"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/symmetric-hadamard-4356"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  A short note updating one entry of the 2025 Đoković–Seberry census of
  symmetric Hadamard matrices of order 4v, v odd: v = 1089 is listed as
  undecided. No new construction is involved. Wallis and Whiteman (1972) give
  a regular symmetric Hadamard matrix with constant diagonal of order (p-1)^2
  from a symmetric conference matrix of order p-1, p a prime power; Gritsenko
  (2021) supplies a symmetric conference matrix of order 66. With p = 67 this
  gives order 4356 = 4·1089. The repository builds the matrix and checks it
  exactly. Novelty is bounded to the sources searched.
keywords:
  - Hadamard matrices
  - symmetric Hadamard matrices
  - conference matrices
  - strongly regular graphs
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Some classes of Hadamard matrices with constant diagonal"
    authors:
